avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-28T11:41:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-28T11:41:08Z","body":"> On a side note, @m4gr3d What do you think about adding an option to change compileSdkVersion from the editor as well?\n\nI'd rather not since unlike the target AFK version, changing the compile sdk could cause compilation errors that most Godot developers would be unfamiliar with. And having both options would be confusing for Godot developers unfamiliar with Android.\n\nWhat would be the reason for a Godot developer to change the compile sdk version?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343021342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343381457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110081#issuecomment-3343381457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110081","id":3343381457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7HR_PR","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-28T13:31:21Z","updated_at":"2025-09-28T13:31:21Z","body":"It’s mainly for users who are familiar with Android development. They might use it when modifying gradle build template the, since sometimes you also need to update the compile sdk. Generally, we keep the compile sdk and target sdk at the same version; having the target sdk higher than the compile sdk can cause runtime errors that would otherwise have been caught at compile time. That said, compilesdk can still be changed manually; I was just wondering about it.\n\nComing back to the issue: the manifest mentions compile sdk 34, so I think the OP might have mistaken it for the target SDK.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3343381457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godo